Dear Students,

Please note the following important instructions regarding the Final CP/MP =
Viva:

1.      All students must prepare the final project report and other requir=
ed documents as per the given checklist and submit them to their respective=
 supervisors for verification by 14th May 2026.

2.      Once verified, each student must take printouts of two hard-bound c=
opies of the final project report - one for personal record and one for the=
 supervisor. The hard-bound report cover page must be in Blue colour with G=
olden embossing.

3.      For MP students, only one hard-bound copy for the supervisor needs =
to be submitted for the entire group, while each student must maintain one =
personal hard-bound copy. In the personal copy, the respective student's na=
me should appear in the first position, and the names of the other group me=
mbers should follow.

4.      All students must obtain the signature of the supervisor on all har=
d copies of the documents and the checklist before the Final Viva.

5.      Students must upload the soft copies of the verified documents as p=
er the checklist by 18th May 2026. (The upload link will be shared shortly.)

6.      The Similarity Index (Plagiarism Report) and AI Plagiarism Report o=
f the project report must be below 10%. The summary pages of both reports m=
ust be attached at the end of the final project report.

7.      Students who have not completed their internship by 19th May 2026 m=
ust submit either: a certificate of progress, or an email confirmation from=
 the industry supervisor clearly mentioning the expected date of completion.

8.      The viva will begin at 9:00 AM sharp. All students must be present =
at the venue well in advance. The detailed schedule and venue will be share=
d shortly.

9.      Each student must prepare a PowerPoint presentation covering the fo=
llowing:

*                Problem Statement

*                Objectives

*                Methodology

*                Results

*                Conclusions

*                Research Outcomes (Publications/Patents, if any)

*                References

10.  Please note the following details while preparing the final report: Th=
e degree name should be written as: BACHELOR OF TECHNOLOGY IN COMPUTER ENGI=
NEERING. The department name should be written as: COMPUTER SCIENCE & ENGIN=
EERING

Please adhere to all the above guidelines carefully to ensure a smooth and =
successful viva process.

For any queries, kindly contact your respective supervisor.
Dr. Sidheswar Routray
Assistant Professor,
Department of Computer Engineering,
School of Technology,
Pandit Deendayal Energy University,
Gandhinagar, Gujarat 382007.
